{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP-03 finite-pass fuse history checkpoint (2026-08-17/18). Full Reconcile Bridge inventory: 11,445 terminal runs from 2026-06-25 through 2026-08-18 (9,666 success, 415 failure, 1 startup failure, 1,363 cancelled; 934 main SHAs). No workflow was dispatched. Clean replay slice indexes 2400-3599 covers 1,200 completed runs from 2026-07-26 through 2026-08-02: 1,182 success / 18 failure, 1,193 with mutation outcomes, zero terminal transient failures, zero 3-consecutive or 5-of-10 openings, and zero success after a simulated opening. Run 31653436625 proves intermediate observation timeouts must not count: bulk comment REST timed out, per-ticket fallback healed it, all 11 mutations completed, pass converged. Runs 30777393799 and 30771959736 each had dozens of successes plus one literal ACLI unknown error; unknown diagnostics must not be guessed into a provider fuse. Known 404 partial passes remain permanent ticket-isolation evidence. Six Aug 7-11 auth failures recorded on sole-curbable-stinkpot failed the first Jira call and should use authoritative credential/pass scope, not inference. Maintained GitLab/Sentry/pycontribs/atlassian-python-api/Mattermost integrations use request/task-local retry and no cross-ticket Jira breaker; the scoped fuse is Rebar-specific. Detailed evolving note: .joe-janitor/rp03-fuse-history-validation.md. Remaining work: all-failure replay plus remaining successful slices and a decision on whether rolling 5-of-10 has enough evidence."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787019985800640001,"uuid":"bced3dfa-08ed-4bec-95b1-50966a0d9f3d"}